  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Facing the Toulon Yacht Club, in the Mourillon area, Anse Tabarly is the city's first purpose-built dog beach. A ramp specially dedicated to dogs for reaching the water makes swimming easy, including for older dogs or ones not fully at ease in the water.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access is free and open every day of the year, with no seasonal restriction. It's a swimming alternative to the nearby Mourillon beaches, where dogs on a leash are only tolerated on the Promenade Henri-Fabre (not on the sand).</p>
      <p>Worth knowing for the future: according to an interview with Toulon's mayor published in the city's own magazine (Toulon Magazine n°1, May-June 2026), the city planned the Pipady dog beach partly in anticipation of eventually closing Anse Tabarly, which is meant to make way for a future marina/nautical base project. Pipady did open on 1 July 2026, but as of autumn 2026 Anse Tabarly is still in service (the official Mourillon beach regulation still references it): no closing date is known yet, so it's worth checking if you're planning a long-term visit.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: there are no hours to remember here — your dog can swim at any time of day, all year round — but this site could close eventually; the nearby Pipady dog beach is the safer long-term bet if you're unsure.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Mourillon beaches and their long promenade are just around the corner, as is Toulon's second dog beach, Pipady, at the foot of the Tour Royale.</p>
    </div>

